  "question": {
    "text": "A liquid is flowing through a non-sectional tube with its axis horizontally. If two points $\\mathrm{X}$ and $\\mathrm{Y}$ on the axis of tube has a sectional area $2.0 \\mathrm{~cm}^{3}$ and $25 \\mathrm{~mm}^{2}$ respectively then find the flow velocity at $Y$ when the flow velocity at $X$ is $10 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "nXki4",
      "text": "$20 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ePmxX",
      "text": "$40 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TYewQ",
      "text": "$80 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "rgZh8",
      "text": "$60 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "According to principle of continuity\n$$\nv_{y}=\\frac{v_{x} A_{x}}{A_{y}}=\\frac{10(m / s) \\times 2\\left(c m^{2}\\right)}{25 \\times 10^{-2}\\left(c m^{2}\\right)}=80 \\mathrm{~m} / \\mathrm{s}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
